{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And to those who keep His commandments to a thousand generations.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Sotah 31a) that for those who act from fear the reward is לאלף דור, while for those who act from love it is אלפים, as it says (Exodus 20:6): ״וְעֹשֶׂה חֶסֶד לַאֲלָפִים לְאֹהֲבַי״ and so forth. And it appears that not doubling alone is what אלפים indicates, for certainly for one who acts from love there is no end to the reward of his deeds, and the plural form אלפים said regarding those who love Him — we could say it means even up to a hundred thousand. And the reason it says this without specification is that there is no fixed measure for love, and between one lover and another there are multiples upon multiples; rather, the smallest among the lovers is double the greatest among those who fear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:40.368686576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}